+/// \brief Recover the physical address represented by a segmented symbol expression
+///
+/// A PTRSUB that names a symbol can still retain the original far-pointer encoding
+/// as its constant input.  The symbol mapping is already the resolved physical
+/// location, so attach it when it differs from the printed expression's encoding.
+Address PrintC::getResolvedSymbolAddress(const Symbol *sym,const PcodeOp *op) const
